(2613004, 358398, 42013, '<td valign="top">ONe of my favorites from this challenge. The only think i didn''t care for was the dead center crop on the guy. But, only a small nitpic, otherwise great job!</td>', 'ONe of my favorites from this challenge. The only think i didn''t care for was the dead center crop on the guy. But, only a small nitpic, otherwise great job!', '2006-07-12 01:35:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613005, 356042, 27735, '<td valign="top">The submitted version was edited on my laptop -- that''s why the colors are so extreme. Here''s another version...<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=361391" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361391.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361391.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361391.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Here are a couple more taken from the same dock as the one above...<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=361389" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361389.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361389.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361389.jpg"/></a> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=361392" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361392.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361392.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/27735/thumb/361392.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>All these shots were taken on the west side of Lake Tahoe near Homewood. I got there at 5:30 AM, just before sunrise. Pretty much all of the photos from this series were taken while holding two graduated neutral density filters in front of the lens.<br/> <br/>Oh yeah, they were all taken with the EF-S 10-22mm lens.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-12 00:36:49.</i></td>', 'The submitted version was edited on my laptop -- that''s why the colors are so extreme. Here''s another version...  Here are a couple more taken from the same dock as the one above...   All these shots were taken on the west side of Lake Tahoe near Homewood. I got there at 5:30 AM, just before sunrise. Pretty much all of the photos from this series were taken while holding two graduated neutral density filters in front of the lens. Oh yeah, they were all taken with the EF-S 10-22mm lens.', '2006-07-12 01:35:27.000000', '2006-07-12 01:36:49.000000', 0),
(2613065, 358196, 53147, '<td valign="top">Hated to have to pull down so far to find this shots placement. And how could I have not guessed this to be yours? Again - great shot. I love it alot. You was robbed!  :)</td>', 'Hated to have to pull down so far to find this shots placement. And how could I have not guessed this to be yours? Again - great shot. I love it alot. You was robbed!  :)', '2006-07-12 01:42:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613077, 358137, 5112, '<td valign="top">Þorsteinn, congratulations on your well deserved blue with this strong image.  Love the contrast between the wood/earth tones and the sky.  The clouds are beautiful to look at.</td>', 'Þorsteinn, congratulations on your well deserved blue with this strong image.  Love the contrast between the wood/earth tones and the sky.  The clouds are beautiful to look at.', '2006-07-12 01:44:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613106, 358566, 29753, '<td valign="top">this is fantastic!!!!!!</td>', 'this is fantastic!!!!!!', '2006-07-12 01:47:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613181, 358518, 50231, '<td valign="top">Nice Buddy! Good finish!</td>', 'Nice Buddy! Good finish!', '2006-07-12 01:57:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613227, 356171, 59343, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mpeters:</b></div><hr/><i> Good finish! As I said before, the tones in this picture work well. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Mpeters and everyone else who liked my image.  I thought it was good--a little surprised though at my finish--wasn''t expecting this high of a finish--there are truly some amazing pictures out there.<br/> <br/>@kemptonreporter--I agree that this was the wrong time of day--but I couldn''t do much about it.  It seemed to do ok anyway.<br/> <br/>With regards to the comment being off balance...for future reference I was wondering what made it off balance--the extra space in front of the boat, or the leaning of the boat.  <br/> <br/>Thanks again.</td>', 'Originally posted by mpeters: Good finish! As I said before, the tones in this picture work well.   Thanks Mpeters and everyone else who liked my image.  I thought it was good--a little surprised though at my finish--wasn''t expecting this high of a finish--there are truly some amazing pictures out there. @kemptonreporter--I agree that this was the wrong time of day--but I couldn''t do much about it.  It seemed to do ok anyway. With regards to the comment being off balance...for future reference I was wondering what made it off balance--the extra space in front of the boat, or the leaning of the boat.   Thanks again.', '2006-07-12 02:02:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613229, 354880, 57358, '<td valign="top">(ouch, awesome photo but I don''t think layers are allowed in basic)  I love the setup and your colors, congrats on such an awesome score</td>', '(ouch, awesome photo but I don''t think layers are allowed in basic)  I love the setup and your colors, congrats on such an awesome score', '2006-07-12 02:03:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613233, 358566, 42916, '<td valign="top">This should have placed much higher. Haters out there that vote for stuff that doesn''t really fit the subject of the challenge but it just a nice photo. No surprise really. Still top 30 finish is good :)</td>', 'This should have placed much higher. Haters out there that vote for stuff that doesn''t really fit the subject of the challenge but it just a nice photo. No surprise really. Still top 30 finish is good :)', '2006-07-12 02:04:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613236, 354880, 10485, '<td valign="top">Sorry guys....this is my first submission and I was really excited to see I placed 5th and then was asked for proof,which I happily sent. Then read comments from "djborjabor" and went back to look at diff between basic and advanced editing !! I apologize to all who voted. I read that cloning is an absolute no-no.....and I used to to clone out a small sign ! Oh well, I should have read more closely...thanks for all the comments though....hope in the future I can place in top ten....adhering strictly to the different rules...I am now educated.<br/>thanks guys.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-12 01:06:03.</i></td>', 'Sorry guys....this is my first submission and I was really excited to see I placed 5th and then was asked for proof,which I happily sent. Then read comments from "djborjabor" and went back to look at diff between basic and advanced editing !! I apologize to all who voted. I read that cloning is an absolute no-no.....and I used to to clone out a small sign ! Oh well, I should have read more closely...thanks for all the comments though....hope in the future I can place in top ten....adhering strictly to the different rules...I am now educated.thanks guys.', '2006-07-12 02:05:09.000000', '2006-07-12 02:06:03.000000', 0),
