(2613502, 356706, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Qiki:</b></div><hr/><i> Lovely shot Lev. Someone has to ask though....conisering the 1/3000 shutter speed, were the turbines actually stationary (''No Wind'')? :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Adrian,<br/>to tell you the truth, a few turbines were spinning, not fast, but some... :). I hope it is not a reasan for DQ :). 1/3000 was not because of that, even 1/30 would''ve been sufficient to stop the motion, simply it was still pretty early and light, and I was shooting right into the sunset.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-12 02:03:36.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Qiki: Lovely shot Lev. Someone has to ask though....conisering the 1/3000 shutter speed, were the turbines actually stationary (''No Wind'')? :)   Adrian,to tell you the truth, a few turbines were spinning, not fast, but some... :). I hope it is not a reasan for DQ :). 1/3000 was not because of that, even 1/30 would''ve been sufficient to stop the motion, simply it was still pretty early and light, and I was shooting right into the sunset.', '2006-07-12 03:03:03.000000', '2006-07-12 03:03:36.000000', 0),
